# The bytes on disk are the bytes in the commit, on every platform.
#
# Windows checks text out with CRLF by default, and this repository's tests read its own source
# and compare it line by line: a `\n` in the expectation against a `\r\n` on disk fails every
# such test on a runner that is otherwise fine. The first Windows build failed exactly that way —
# fifteen interface tests, none of them about Windows. Pinning the ending here is what makes "the
# suite is green" mean the same thing on both runners.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything whose bytes are its meaning keeps its bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.gguf binary
*.dylib binary
